  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="4.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVAtr">IV Atr</ref> 4.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4.2" corresp="#wit-q">Si curet amicitiam ipsius porti, reddat nobis triginta sol. emendationis, si rex hoc concedat nobis.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="4.2" corresp="#wit-q">Si curet amicitiam ipsius porti, reddat nobis triginta sol. emendationis, si rex hoc concedat nobis.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q">If he values the good-will of the town itself, he shall pay us 30 shillings as compensation, if the king will grant us this concession.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Wenn ihm an der Freundschaft dieser Stadt [London] liegt, zahle er uns 30 Schill. Busse, wenn der König uns dies zugestehen will.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If he cares about the friendship of this town [London], let him pay us 30 shillings in compensation, if the king will grant us this.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="235"><ref target="clause:Ine_9">Ine 9</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. Ine 9</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="382"><ref target="clause:Duns_9-1">Duns 9.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares Ine 9.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
